{{#> layout
  title='How to use Vocably in iOS Safari'
  url='/ios-safari-extension.html'
}}
  <section class="ise-hero container-md text-center">
    <span class="ise-eyebrow"><i class="bi bi-apple" aria-hidden="true"></i> Vocably for Safari on iPhone</span>
    <h1 class="ise-title">Translate any word without leaving Safari</h1>
    <p class="ise-lead">
      Select a word on any web page, tap <strong>Look up</strong>, and Vocably
      shows the translation and saves it to your cards. Setting it up takes
      about two minutes.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="container-md">
    <ol class="ise-steps">
      <li class="ise-step">
        <div class="ise-step-body">
          <span class="ise-step-number" aria-hidden="true">1</span>
          <h2>Install the Vocably app</h2>
          <p>
            The Safari extension comes with the Vocably app. Install it from the
            App Store, or update it if you already have it.
          </p>
          <a
            href="https://apps.apple.com/app/vocably-pro-language-cards/id1641258757"
            target="_blank"
            class="d-inline-block mt-2"
            data-umami-event="iOS Safari Extension CTA Click"
            data-umami-event-label="iOS"
          ><img src="assets/download-on-app-store.svg" alt="Download on the App Store" height="48" /></a>
        </div>
      </li>

      <li class="ise-step">
        <div class="ise-step-body">
          <span class="ise-step-number" aria-hidden="true">2</span>
          <h2>Turn on the extension</h2>
          <p>
            Open <strong>Settings&nbsp;→ Safari&nbsp;→ Extensions</strong>
            and tap <strong>Vocably for Safari</strong>.
          </p>
          <p class="ise-hint">
            On iOS&nbsp;18 and later, Safari is under
            <strong>Settings&nbsp;→ Apps&nbsp;→ Safari</strong>.
          </p>
          <ul class="ise-checklist">
            <li><i class="bi bi-check-circle-fill" aria-hidden="true"></i> <span>Switch on <strong>Allow Extension</strong>.</span></li>
            <li><i class="bi bi-check-circle-fill" aria-hidden="true"></i> <span>Set <strong>vocably.pro</strong> to <strong>Allow</strong>, so you can sign in to your account.</span></li>
          </ul>
          <div class="ise-note">
            <i class="bi bi-shield-check" aria-hidden="true"></i>
            <p>
              Optionally, set <strong>Other Websites</strong> to
              <strong>Allow</strong> as well, and Vocably will work on every
              site with no extra steps. The extension is
              <a href="https://github.com/vocably/language-learning-tool/tree/main/packages/ios-extension" target="_blank">open source</a>,
              so you can check what it does.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <figure class="ise-step-media">
          <video loop autoplay muted playsinline controls class="ise-phone" width="1178" height="2556">
            <source src="assets/ios-safari-extension/enable-extension.mp4" type="video/mp4" />
          </video>
        </figure>
      </li>

      <li class="ise-step">
        <div class="ise-step-body">
          <span class="ise-step-number" aria-hidden="true">3</span>
          <h2>Allow Vocably on a website</h2>
          <p class="ise-hint">
            Skip this step if you allowed Other Websites in step&nbsp;2.
          </p>
          <p>
            Open the website you want to read in Safari and tap the puzzle
            icon (<i class="bi bi-puzzle" aria-label="puzzle"></i>) in the
            address bar.
          </p>
          <p>
            Tap <strong>Manage Extensions</strong> and switch on
            <strong>Vocably for Safari</strong>.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="ise-step-media ise-step-media-pair">
          <figure>
            <img src="assets/ios-safari-extension/puzzle-button.png" class="ise-phone" width="400" height="867" alt="The puzzle icon in the Safari address bar." loading="lazy" />
            <figcaption>Tap the puzzle icon</figcaption>
          </figure>
          <figure>
            <img src="assets/ios-safari-extension/enable-extension.png" class="ise-phone" width="400" height="867" alt="Vocably for Safari switched on in Manage Extensions." loading="lazy" />
            <figcaption>Switch on Vocably</figcaption>
          </figure>
        </div>
      </li>

      <li class="ise-step">
        <div class="ise-step-body">
          <span class="ise-step-number" aria-hidden="true">4</span>
          <h2>Select a word and look it up</h2>
          <p>
            Select any word on the page. A <strong>Look up</strong> button
            with the Vocably logo appears at the bottom of the screen. Tap it
            to see the translation and add the word to your cards.
          </p>
          <p class="ise-hint">
            Use the Vocably button, not the <strong>Look Up</strong> item in
            the iOS text menu.
          </p>
        </div>
        <figure class="ise-step-media">
          <img src="assets/ios-safari-extension/select-and-lookup.png" class="ise-phone" width="400" height="867" alt="A selected word and the Vocably Look up button below it." loading="lazy" />
        </figure>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="container-md ise-help-section">
    <div class="ise-help">
      <i class="bi bi-envelope-heart" aria-hidden="true"></i>
      <div>
        <h2>Stuck somewhere?</h2>
        <p>
          Write to me at <a href="mailto:d@vocably.pro">d@vocably.pro</a>.
          I read and answer every email.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
{{/layout}}
